## Why This Is Asked
Interleaves real-world concurrency challenges: per-key in-order guarantees, bounded buffers, dynamic worker pools, and backpressure under bursts. Tests deep understanding of ordering, backpressure signaling, and load repartitioning.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key (cell) in-order processing
- Bounded per-key FIFOs
- Dispatcher with stable routing (consistent hashing)
- Per-key reordering buffers
- Global in-flight limiter with backpressure and dynamic rebalance

## Code Example
```javascript
class CellState {
  constructor() {
    this.lastSeq = 0;
    thisbuffer = new Map(); // cell_id -> [msgs in order]
  }
  handle(msg){
    const {cell_id, seq} = msg;
    const s = this.state.get(cell_id) || {lastSeq:0, buf:[]};
    if(seq === s.lastSeq+1){
      s.lastSeq = seq;
      this.emit(msg);
      // drain buffered contiguous msgs
    } else {
      s.buf.push(msg);
      // keep bounded and sort by seq for reordering
    }
    this.state.set(cell_id, s);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test correctness when late events arrive after many already-processed messages?
- What backpressure signals would you expose to upstream systems and how would you prevent starvation during rebalance?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design simple concurrent systems with cancellation semantics, ordering guarantees, and backpressure within a bounded queue.

## Key Concepts

- Cancellation tokens attached to tasks
- Per-service FIFO buffers
- Global bounded work queue
- Worker coordination and cancellation checks
- Backpressure and graceful shutdown

## Code Example

```go
type Event struct {
  Data   string
  Cancel <-chan struct{}
}

func worker(id int, queue <-chan Event, done <-chan struct{}) {
  for {
    select {
    case e := <-queue:
      select {
      case <-e.Cancel:
        // canceled before processing
        continue
      default:
        process(e)
      }
    case <-done:
      return
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ensure per-service ordering if cancellation is frequent?
- How would you test backpressure behavior under bursty producers?

